# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local development. All three variables
# are public/build-time (Next.js inlines any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable into the
# client bundle), so never put secrets in any of them.
#
# The privacy version and URL below are approved public values, not secrets.
# The API hostname remains deliberately unset until it is approved.

# Base URL of the real backend waitlist API, no trailing slash. The frontend
# posts to `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL}/waitlist`. NOT YET APPROVED — replace
# with the actual backend host once one exists and has been confirmed; do not
# fill this in with a guess.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend-host.example

# Must match the approved privacy-policy version expected by the backend.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_VERSION=2026-08-23

# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL previously lived here as an override for the
# lead-form consent link. Removed: /privacy/waitlist is now a real internal
# route (src/lib/waitlist-privacy-policy-config.ts), so the consent link
# points at it directly and no longer needs a URL supplied via env var.
#
# The website/waitlist-scoped policy proposes version 2026-08-26 (see
# waitlist-privacy-policy.md) but this env var above must NOT be bumped to
# that value until legal has approved it AND the backend's own
# PRIVACY_POLICY_VERSION has been updated to match exactly - they must
# always agree, or every submission is rejected (see waitlist.ts).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The static website/ implementation is plain HTML/JS (no Next.js build
# step), so it cannot read process.env at all. It reads the equivalent three
# values from its own <script type="text/x-dc" data-props="..."> block
# instead: "apiBaseUrl", "privacyPolicyVersion", "privacyPolicyUrl" (all
# use approved privacy defaults in website/index.html; apiBaseUrl stays empty).
#
# How those get set for the currently-live static page is NOT something this
# repo controls or documents elsewhere: the file's <x-dc>/data-dc-script
# markup and the "DC" runtime it loads (website/assets/c18fe535-*.js) both
# indicate this page is exported by an external site-builder tool, not
# hand-deployed from this checkout. This repo has no CI/deploy config for
# website/ and no visibility into that tool's publish flow. Concretely, one
# of two things must be true before real values reach the live page, and
# nothing here confirms which:
#   (a) the three prop defaults are edited directly in the data-props JSON
#       in website/index.html before that file is deployed as-is, or
#   (b) they're set through that external tool's own prop-editing UI before
#       it re-exports this page — in which case editing the checked-in HTML
#       directly would be overwritten on the next export.
# Confirm which applies with whoever owns that tool/deployment before
# shipping real values — this is flagged as a launch blocker in the report.
